{"id":"gcse-heart-circulation","title":"GCSE Biology: the heart and circulation","subject":"Biology","label":"GCSE","exams":["gcse"],"language":"en","seconds":166,"duration":166,"audio":"voice.mp3","words":453,"sections":[{"id":"hook","title":"Everyday puzzle","start":0,"end":15.405},{"id":"explain","title":"Core idea","start":15.405,"end":38.435},{"id":"explain2","title":"Blood route","start":38.435,"end":89.935},{"id":"example","title":"Worked example","start":89.935,"end":109.535},{"id":"check","title":"Quick check","start":109.535,"end":117.915},{"id":"answer","title":"Answer","start":117.915,"end":124.145},{"id":"mistakes","title":"Common mistakes","start":124.145,"end":144.005},{"id":"recap","title":"Recap","start":144.005,"end":166}],"lines":[{"s":0,"a":0.5,"b":3.65,"text":"Have you ever felt your heart pound after running for a bus?","w":[0.56,0.72,0.86,1.12,1.38,1.56,1.84,2.34,2.62,2.92,3.1,3.18]},{"s":0,"a":4.1,"b":9.62,"text":"That pounding is your heart, a muscular pump, working hard to move blood around your body.","w":[4.16,4.46,4.98,5.08,5.26,6.1,6.22,6.76,7.44,7.84,8.14,8.26,8.52,8.8,9.08,9.24]},{"s":0,"a":9.92,"b":14.98,"text":"I'm Kora. In the next three minutes, you'll see why it beats and where your blood goes.","w":[10.02,10.2,11.02,11.12,11.24,11.46,11.7,12.44,12.7,12.94,13.18,13.3,13.72,13.84,14.08,14.24,14.5]},{"s":1,"a":15.83,"b":18.54,"text":"The heart is a muscular pump with four chambers.","w":[15.86,16.04,16.4,16.52,16.66,17.16,17.48,17.72,18.02]},{"s":1,"a":18.84,"b":22.16,"text":"Two atria sit on top, and two ventricles sit below.","w":[18.9,19.14,19.6,19.8,19.9,20.5,20.68,20.94,21.56,21.78]},{"s":1,"a":22.46,"b":25.53,"text":"The atria receive blood, and the ventricles pump it out.","w":[22.46,22.64,23.04,23.48,24.22,24.34,24.44,24.98,25.24,25.36]},{"s":1,"a":25.83,"b":28.78,"text":"The right side pumps deoxygenated blood to your lungs.","w":[25.84,26,26.28,26.62,26.96,27.74,28.02,28.14,28.32]},{"s":1,"a":29.08,"b":32.59,"text":"The left side pumps oxygenated blood to the rest of your body.","w":[29.1,29.28,29.6,30.04,30.56,31.22,31.56,31.68,31.82,32.04,32.12,32.28]},{"s":1,"a":32.89,"b":38.01,"text":"So blood passes through the heart twice per circuit. That is your double circulatory system.","w":[32.96,33.2,33.58,34,34.22,34.32,34.62,35.04,35.24,36.1,36.32,36.4,36.58,36.96,37.66]},{"s":2,"a":38.86,"b":50.34,"text":"Follow one drop through the vena cava, right atrium, right ventricle, pulmonary artery, lungs, pulmonary vein, left atrium, left ventricle, aorta, body.","w":[38.96,39.48,39.64,39.94,40.16,40.26,40.56,41.44,41.74,42.7,42.92,43.76,44.4,45.16,45.84,46.4,47.1,47.48,48.22,48.52,49.22,49.94]},{"s":2,"a":50.64,"b":53.12,"text":"Valves stop blood flowing backwards.","w":[50.72,51.22,51.76,52.16,52.54]},{"s":2,"a":53.42,"b":58.47,"text":"The left ventricle wall is thicker because it pumps blood all the way round your body at higher pressure.","w":[53.44,53.58,53.88,54.36,54.7,54.86,55.22,55.52,55.64,56,56.46,56.62,56.74,56.92,57.16,57.3,57.7,57.82,58.12]},{"s":2,"a":58.77,"b":63.71,"text":"Arteries carry blood away from the heart. They have thick muscular walls and high pressure.","w":[58.86,59.34,59.68,59.96,60.24,60.38,60.5,61.28,61.44,61.68,61.94,62.42,62.84,63,63.24]},{"s":2,"a":64.01,"b":67.55,"text":"Veins carry blood back. They have valves and thinner walls.","w":[64.1,64.46,64.8,65.06,65.76,65.96,66.16,66.58,66.74,67.04]},{"s":2,"a":67.85,"b":70.54,"text":"Capillaries are one cell thick for exchange.","w":[67.9,68.7,68.96,69.2,69.5,69.78,69.96]},{"s":2,"a":70.84,"b":75.83,"text":"The two sides are separated, so oxygenated and deoxygenated blood do not mix.","w":[70.86,71,71.24,71.62,71.76,72.7,73,73.82,73.96,74.78,75.08,75.22,75.4]},{"s":2,"a":76.13,"b":81.78,"text":"The pulmonary artery carries deoxygenated blood, and the pulmonary vein carries oxygenated blood.","w":[76.18,76.34,77,77.32,77.68,78.44,79.24,79.36,79.5,80.1,80.44,80.86,81.46]},{"s":2,"a":82.08,"b":84.6,"text":"Coronary arteries supply the heart muscle itself.","w":[82.14,82.7,83.14,83.56,83.66,83.92,84.22]},{"s":2,"a":84.9,"b":89.51,"text":"A natural pacemaker, a group of cells in the right atrium, sets the rhythm.","w":[84.96,85.08,85.54,86.58,86.68,86.96,87.12,87.46,87.56,87.68,87.98,88.78,89.1,89.22]},{"s":3,"a":90.36,"b":92.6,"text":"Let's trace a drop from the right ventricle.","w":[90.42,90.72,91.04,91.14,91.52,91.7,91.82,92.1]},{"s":3,"a":92.9,"b":95.62,"text":"It leaves through the pulmonary artery to the lungs.","w":[93,93.14,93.56,93.8,93.9,94.52,94.88,95,95.12]},{"s":3,"a":95.92,"b":97.42,"text":"There it picks up oxygen.","w":[95.94,96.28,96.4,96.7,96.94]},{"s":3,"a":97.72,"b":100.9,"text":"It returns through the pulmonary vein to the left atrium.","w":[97.8,97.9,98.46,98.72,98.84,99.44,99.78,99.92,100.04,100.38]},{"s":3,"a":101.2,"b":104.94,"text":"Then it goes to the left ventricle and out through the aorta to the body.","w":[101.26,101.5,101.6,101.88,102,102.14,102.4,103.18,103.44,103.58,103.8,103.92,104.38,104.5,104.6]},{"s":3,"a":105.24,"b":109.11,"text":"From the body it returns in the vena cava, completing the double circuit.","w":[105.3,105.5,105.64,106.06,106.18,106.64,106.72,106.82,107.1,107.8,108.34,108.46,108.78]},{"s":4,"a":109.96,"b":115,"text":"Quick check. Why is the wall of the left ventricle thicker than the wall of the right ventricle?","w":[109.98,110.26,111,111.28,111.42,111.58,111.96,112.06,112.18,112.46,113.04,113.42,113.58,113.7,114.06,114.16,114.3,114.54]},{"s":4,"a":115.45,"b":117.49,"text":"Pause here and try it. I'll wait.","w":[115.5,115.82,116.12,116.26,116.54,116.94,117.14]},{"s":5,"a":118.34,"b":123.72,"text":"The left ventricle wall is thicker because it pumps blood all the way round the body at higher pressure.","w":[118.38,118.52,118.82,119.32,119.72,119.92,120.4,120.72,120.86,121.26,121.72,121.88,122,122.18,122.44,122.54,122.96,123.08,123.36]},{"s":6,"a":124.57,"b":132.03,"text":"One common mistake is saying all arteries carry oxygenated blood. Remember, the pulmonary artery carries deoxygenated blood.","w":[124.74,124.92,125.26,125.68,125.8,126.2,126.46,126.9,127.32,127.96,128.74,129.5,129.62,130.22,130.56,130.94,131.7]},{"s":6,"a":132.33,"b":137.6,"text":"Another is mixing up left and right. On a diagram, the heart's right side is on your left.","w":[132.42,132.78,132.92,133.24,133.44,133.72,133.86,134.62,134.72,134.8,135.62,135.78,136.14,136.38,136.8,136.94,137.04,137.22]},{"s":6,"a":137.9,"b":143.58,"text":"Never say the heart makes oxygenated blood. It only pumps blood, and the lungs add oxygen.","w":[138.02,138.32,138.5,138.66,138.94,139.28,139.9,140.56,140.74,141,141.4,142.12,142.24,142.4,142.86,143.12]},{"s":7,"a":144.43,"b":147.89,"text":"The heart has four chambers and pumps blood twice per circuit.","w":[144.44,144.58,144.84,145.08,145.38,146.02,146.2,146.62,146.96,147.34,147.54]},{"s":7,"a":148.19,"b":151.94,"text":"The right side goes to the lungs, and the left side goes to the body.","w":[148.22,148.38,148.64,148.94,149.18,149.34,149.48,150.26,150.4,150.54,150.82,151.18,151.4,151.54,151.62]},{"s":7,"a":152.24,"b":156.67,"text":"Valves stop backflow, and the left ventricle is thicker for higher pressure.","w":[152.3,152.94,153.32,154.16,154.28,154.42,154.72,155.32,155.48,155.84,156,156.3]},{"s":7,"a":156.97,"b":161.07,"text":"Exam tip: learn the route in order, and the two pulmonary exceptions.","w":[157.06,157.46,158.02,158.28,158.4,158.66,158.78,159.38,159.5,159.64,159.88,160.42]},{"s":7,"a":161.37,"b":165.4,"text":"Knowzone is here whenever you want to revise this again. You're doing well.","w":[161.46,161.98,162.12,162.38,162.74,162.9,163.1,163.22,163.62,163.82,164.6,164.8,165.1]}],"scenes":[{"at":0.25,"heading":"Heart: a pump","items":[{"at":0.4,"kind":"text","text":"Heart pounds after running for a bus?"},{"at":4,"kind":"term","text":"Heart","detail":"Muscular pump moving blood around body"},{"at":9.82,"kind":"text","text":"Why it beats; where blood goes"}]},{"at":15.58,"heading":"Heart: four chambers","items":[{"at":15.73,"kind":"term","text":"Heart","detail":"Muscular pump with four chambers"},{"at":15.73,"kind":"image","text":"The heart. Blue: deoxygenated blood. Red: oxygenated","src":"heart.webp","credit":"ZooFari · CC BY-SA 3.0 · Wikimedia Commons"},{"at":18.74,"kind":"text","text":"2 atria on top; 2 ventricles below"}]},{"at":22.21,"heading":"Chambers and sides","items":[{"at":22.36,"kind":"term","text":"Atria","detail":"Receive blood"},{"at":22.36,"kind":"term","text":"Ventricles","detail":"Pump blood out"},{"at":25.73,"kind":"text","text":"Right side → lungs: deoxygenated blood"},{"at":28.98,"kind":"text","text":"Left side → body: oxygenated blood"},{"at":32.79,"kind":"term","text":"Double circulatory system","detail":"Blood passes through heart twice per circuit"}]},{"at":38.61,"heading":"Blood route","items":[{"at":38.76,"kind":"text","text":"Vena cava → right atrium → right ventricle"},{"at":38.76,"kind":"text","text":"Pulmonary artery → lungs → pulmonary vein"},{"at":38.76,"kind":"text","text":"Left atrium → left ventricle → aorta → body"},{"at":38.76,"kind":"image","text":"The heart. Blue: deoxygenated blood. Red: oxygenated","src":"heart.webp","credit":"ZooFari · CC BY-SA 3.0 · Wikimedia Commons"},{"at":50.54,"kind":"term","text":"Valves","detail":"Stop blood flowing backwards"},{"at":53.32,"kind":"text","text":"Left ventricle wall thicker"}]},{"at":58.52,"heading":"Vessels","items":[{"at":58.67,"kind":"term","text":"Arteries","detail":"Carry blood away; thick muscular walls; high pressure"},{"at":63.91,"kind":"term","text":"Veins","detail":"Carry blood back; valves; thinner walls"},{"at":67.75,"kind":"term","text":"Capillaries","detail":"One cell thick for exchange"}]},{"at":70.59,"heading":"Sides and pacemaker","items":[{"at":70.74,"kind":"text","text":"Sides separated → no mixing of blood"},{"at":76.03,"kind":"term","text":"Pulmonary artery","detail":"Deoxygenated; pulmonary vein carries oxygenated"},{"at":81.98,"kind":"term","text":"Coronary arteries","detail":"Supply the heart muscle itself"},{"at":84.8,"kind":"term","text":"Pacemaker","detail":"Cells in right atrium set the rhythm"}]},{"at":90.11,"heading":"Worked example: route","items":[{"at":92.8,"kind":"text","text":"Right ventricle → pulmonary artery → lungs"},{"at":95.82,"kind":"text","text":"Lungs: picks up oxygen"},{"at":97.62,"kind":"text","text":"→ pulmonary vein → left atrium"},{"at":101.1,"kind":"text","text":"→ left ventricle → aorta → body"},{"at":105.14,"kind":"text","text":"Back via vena cava: double circuit complete"}]},{"at":109.53,"heading":"Quick check","items":[{"at":109.53,"kind":"question","text":"Why is the wall of the left ventricle thicker than the wall of the right ventricle?"}]},{"at":118.09,"heading":"Answer","items":[{"at":118.24,"kind":"text","text":"Left ventricle wall is thicker"},{"at":118.24,"kind":"text","text":"Pumps blood round body at higher pressure"}]},{"at":124.32,"heading":"Common mistakes","items":[{"at":124.47,"kind":"wrong","text":"All arteries carry oxygenated blood"},{"at":132.23,"kind":"wrong","text":"Heart's right side is on your right"},{"at":137.8,"kind":"wrong","text":"The heart makes oxygenated blood"}]},{"at":144.18,"heading":"Recap","items":[{"at":144.33,"kind":"text","text":"4 chambers; blood passes twice per circuit"},{"at":148.09,"kind":"text","text":"Right side → lungs; left side → body"},{"at":152.14,"kind":"text","text":"Valves stop backflow; left ventricle thicker"},{"at":156.87,"kind":"tip","text":"Learn the route in order, and the two pulmonary exceptions."},{"at":161.27,"kind":"text","text":"Knowzone: revise this again"}]}],"check":{"at":117.74,"seconds":10,"question":"Why is the wall of the left ventricle thicker than the wall of the right ventricle?","answer":"The left ventricle wall is thicker because it pumps blood all the way round the body at higher pressure."},"fps":30,"mouth":"","level":"","credits":[{"title":"Heart diagram-en.svg","author":"ZooFari","licence":"CC BY-SA 3.0","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Heart_diagram-en.svg"}],"voice":"qwen3-tts-12hz-1.7b (cloned voice)"}